          "profileName": "Adenike A",
          "createdAt": "2026-01-04",
          "starRatings": 5,
          "reviewDetails": "We took the kids to see what a conservation Center looks like. We saw the monkeys and crocodile, walked the 2.4km walk through the forest. It was a nice outing. The tour guides were nice friendly and helpful. They answered the questions the childern asked to give them a better understanding of why the area was protected. It’s a must see and if you’re not afraid of heights then you would definitely love the four level high walks. The experience was well worth it for the family.",
